  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Yasin Istiyak Ahmad Shaikh vs The State Of Maharashtra on 6 March, 2026 Author: N.R. Borkar Bench: N.R. Borkar 2026:Bhc-As:11118 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 568 Of 2026 Yasin Istiyak Ahmad Shaikh ...Applicant V/s. The State of Maharashtra ...Respondent Mr. Tohid Shaikh, Advocate for the Applicant. Mr. B. V. Holambe Patil, App for the Respondent/State. Coram : N.R. Borkar, J. Date : 06.03.2026. P.C. : 2. The applicant is apprehending his arrest in Crime No. 34 of 2026 registered at Kashigaon Police Station, for the offences punishable under Sections 123, 223, 274 & 275 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 26(2)(i), 26(2)(ii), 26(2)(iv), 27(2)(e), 30(2)(a) & 59 of the Food Safety and Standard Act & Section 184 of the Motor Vehicles Act.",
    "facts": "2. The applicant is apprehending his arrest in Crime No. 34 of 2026 registered at Kashigaon Police Station, for the offences punishable under Sections 123, 223, 274 & 275 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 26(2)(i), 26(2)(ii), 26(2)(iv), 27(2)(e), 30(2)(a) & 59 of the Food Safety and Standard Act & Section 184 of the Motor Vehicles Act. Rs.17,04,586/- were found in the possession of the co-accused in the present crime. The allegation against the applicant is that the said prohibited tobacco products were supplied by the present applicant.",
    "arguments": "5. The Hon'ble Supreme Court in the case of Ram Nath vs. The State of Uttar Pradesh1 has observed thus: \"21. .................. ............. ................. .......... ........... We have no manner of doubt that by virtue of Section 89 of the FSSA, Section 59 will override the provisions of Sections 272 and 273 of the IPC.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "5. The Hon'ble Supreme Court in the case of Ram Nath vs. The State of Uttar Pradesh1 has observed thus: \"21. .................. ............. ................. .......... ........... We have no manner of doubt that by virtue of Section 89 of the FSSA, Section 59 will override the provisions of Sections 272 and 273 of the IPC."
